The shaded region under $y=3x$ from $x=0$ to $x=2$ is rotated about the $x$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.4cm, y=0.7cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:2, samples=2, variable=\x] ({\x},{3*\x}) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1,0) -- (3.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.6) -- (0,7.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-0.6:2.4, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{3*\x}) node[pos=0.98, right] {$y=3x$};
\node[below] at (2,-0.2) {$2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region under $y=x+2$ from $x=0$ to $x=3$ is rotated about the $x$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.1cm, y=0.75cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:3, samples=2, variable=\x] ({\x},{\x+2}) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.4,0) -- (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.4) -- (0,6.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.2:3.6, samples=2, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x+2}) node[pos=0.98, right] {$y=x+2$};
\node[below] at (3,-0.2) {$3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region under $y=x^{2}$ from $x=0$ to $x=3$ is rotated about the $x$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.1cm, y=0.42cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:3, samples=60, variable=\x] ({\x},{\x*\x}) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-3.4,0) -- (3.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.8) -- (0,11.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-3.2:3.2, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x}) node[pos=0.98, right] {$y=x^{2}$};
\node[below] at (3,-0.3) {$3$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region under $y=\dfrac{2}{x}$ from $x=1$ to $x=4$ is rotated about the $x$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1cm, y=1cm]
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) -- plot[domain=1:4, samples=80, variable=\x] ({\x},{2/\x}) -- (4,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.6,0) -- (5.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.6) -- (0,4.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=0.5:5.2, samples=80, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{2/\x}) node[pos=0.98, above right] {$y=\frac{2}{x}$};
\node[below] at (1,-0.1) {$1$};
\node[below] at (4,-0.1) {$4$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The shaded region bounded by $y=9-x^{2}$ and the $x$-axis is rotated about the $x$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.7cm, y=0.42cm]
\fill[gray!35] (-3,0) -- plot[domain=-3:3, samples=60, variable=\x] ({\x},{9-\x*\x}) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-4.6,0) -- (4.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.6) -- (0,11.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-3.4:3.4, samples=60, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{9-\x*\x});
\node at (-2.6,10.2) {$y=9-x^{2}$};
\node[below right] at (-3,0) {$-3$};
\node[below left] at (3,0) {$3$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

The shaded region under $y=e^{-x}$ from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is rotated about the $x$-axis.
Find the exact volume of the solid formed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=1.6cm, y=1.6cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- plot[domain=0:1, samples=80, variable=\x] ({\x},{exp(-\x)}) -- (1,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-1.2,0) -- (2.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.6) -- (0,2.8) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-0.9:2.2, samples=80, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{exp(-\x)}) node[pos=0.98, above right] {$y=e^{-x}$};
\node[below] at (1,-0.08) {$1$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
